    "narrative": "For our July 22 slate, **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the charge with a 76.91 score, capitalizing on a premier matchup against Me. Kelly. The +19% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s xERA of 5.31, coupled with a favorable park factor and a spot in the #2 hole, makes him our most efficient play. **James Wood** (71.14) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.64) follow closely, both benefiting from significant park upgrades and ideal spots at the top of their respective orders. While **Corbin Carroll** sits just below the 60-point threshold at 59.77, his dual-threat potential remains vital; however, he is being penalized slightly due to a negative platoon split against the southpaw Jump. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (70.68) and **Isaac Paredes** (65.35) serve as our backbone in the corner infield, both benefiting from favorable R/R platoon dynamics that elevate their output well above their baseline projections.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Naylor**, who landed at 59.86\u2014just a fraction of a point shy of the starting lineup. While his SP-skill bump was promising, his poor BvP history (31 PA) ultimately tipped the scales against him in favor of the more efficient **Austin Riley** (64.43). We are also monitoring the lower-tier starters like **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing** closely; while both are hovering around the 51-point mark, they are currently our best options at catcher. We have successfully avoided the \"below floor\" trap with **Edwin Arroyo**, who was correctly benched at 38.73. With no major weather concerns currently flagged, our primary risk is **Corbin Carroll** and **Austin Riley** facing elite hold scenarios on the basepaths, which\u2014while shaving a few points off their efficiency scores\u2014does not outweigh their overall contribution to our 5x5 needs.",
